# .forge/critical-surfaces — the repo's declaration of files whose wrong change
# fails SILENTLY (crypto signing surfaces, key custody, authz, the dependency-
# direction wall). A slice STAGING a manifest-matched file is T2 through the
# "user declares critical" clause. The critical-surface-gauge commit hook DENIES
# such a commit unless the message carries a `track: T2` trailer (or a deliberate
# FORGE_GAUGE_ACK=1).
#
# This manifest is FORCE-TRACKED (git add -f) past the broad `.forge/` ignore:
# a manifest lost to `git clean -fdx` is a silent gate no-op. The hook itself
# is NOT installed in this repo yet (the manifest ships as documentation; the
# install is an ops follow-on, mirroring verifier application's posture).
#
# Globs match the full repo-relative path. `*` matches any chars including `/`.

# RA1+ — the holder-side signing surface. Private-key handling, deterministic
# signing-input assembly, and compact-envelope framing all fail silently if
# wrong: a key leak, a mis-built signing input, or a malformed envelope still
# produces bytes — the defect surfaces only when a verifier rejects (or worse,
# accepts) downstream. The holder-key-never-leaves-the-edge invariant
# (charter §6) lives here.
lib/bounded_authority_report_adapter/**/*.ex

# RA3 — the dependency-direction wall. The "adapter depends ONLY on the public
# protocol package" invariant (charter §6, strategy §3) is structural; a regression
# here silently re-introduces a private runtime dep and collapses the wall B1
# built in verifier application. The gate that proves it lives here.
test/**/dependency_direction_test.exs

# RA2 — the conformance harness. The harness's value IS its verdict: a wrong
# harness (a vacuous-green round-trip, a mis-built cast_arguments, a shared-nonce
# assumption) ships a broken crypto contract that fails QUIET in production —
# the test passes green locally while the wire format it claims to validate has
# drifted. The harness GUARDS the silent-failure lib/ surface above; a wrong
# harness is itself a silent regression on that surface, so it is declared here
# (design §1.10 C3 — folded into the single enforcement manifest, not a second
# unenforced one). The local test reds noisily, but the production contract it
# certifies fails silent.
test/bounded_authority_report_adapter/conformance_roundtrip_test.exs
